From: djnice <djnice@freemail.hu>
Subject: amvideocap: capture AFBC frames, wait for GE2D, optional HDR to SDR

Video captures through /dev/amvideocap0 came out as garbage or partly
written on S5:

- The source was the VD1 canvas register, which is not updated for an AFBC
  frame without double write (the usual HEVC/VP9/AV1 frame) and may already
  hold the next frame at the frame-end callback. GE2D cannot read AFBC.
- The GE2D blit was queued without waiting and the result copied out right
  away, so a large source (4K double write) was cut off.

The frame-end callback runs in the vsync interrupt, so it now only takes a
copy of the picked vframe and of its linear planes. The conversion runs
afterwards in the reader's context: the planes go into canvases of our own
for a blocking GE2D blit, and an AFBC-only frame is first decompressed and
scaled by VICP into 10-bit 4:4:4 (its 8-bit modes misplace pixel groups).
The current-frame capture now works while paused and reports -ENODATA with
the video layer off.

Colour: GE2D converts with the frame's own matrix (BT.2020, BT.709 or BT.601
from its signal type) instead of always BT.601. An HDR10/HLG source (also the
Dolby Vision profile 8.1 base layer; told by the signal type when the source
format is empty) is mapped to SDR by VICP unless AMVIDEOCAP_IOW_SET_WANTFRAME_TONEMAP
asks to keep its coding; AMVIDEOCAP_IOR_GET_FRAME_TONEMAPPED reports whether
the last frame was mapped.

vicp: the HDR block is programmed with the rest of the configuration, which
is only reloaded when the geometry changes; reload it when the HDR mapping
changes too, else a capture with and one without the mapping in a row both
got the first one's.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
